# Security

- NEVER hardcode API keys, OAuth secrets, or tokens in source code
- Secrets go in `site_config.json` accessed via `frappe.conf`
- OAuth tokens stored using Frappe's Password field type (encrypted at rest)
- Webhook payloads: always verify signatures before processing
- WhatsApp verify_token: read from site_config, never hardcoded
- Gmail API: handle token refresh gracefully, never expose refresh_token
- Log message IDs only — never log full message content
- Parameterized queries only (Frappe ORM handles this, watch raw SQL)
- CORS: whitelist specific origins, never `*` in production
- Rate limit public-facing webhook endpoints
